---
name: bento
description: Bento grid marketing design system skill. Use when building landing pages, feature sections, and portfolios with varied-size grid cells, mixed media, and asymmetric composition.
license: MIT
user-invocable: false
disable-model-invocation: false
---

# Bento Design Spec

Modern marketing grid (Apple, Linear features, Vercel, Raycast): one grid, varied cells, real visual diversity per cell. The anti-"three equal cards" style.

## Core Principles

1. **One Grid, Varied Cells** — Single `grid-template-columns: 2fr 1fr 1fr` (or similar), cells span differently. Never three identical cards in a row.
2. **2–3 Cells Must Differ Visually** — At least 2–3 cells carry image, gradient, pattern, code snippet, or mini-visualization. All-white text cards = fail (see `design-taste/reference/pre-flight.md` Bento rule).
3. **Asymmetry With Collapse** — Desktop asymmetric; below `768px` strict single column (`w-full`, consistent padding). No in-between mush.
4. **One Hero, One Accent** — Hero holds the single bold moment; bento supports with texture, not competing headlines.
5. **Real Content Per Cell** — Each cell answers one question (what / how / proof / CTA). No lorem, no "Jane Doe", no `99.99%` fake stats unless labeled mock.

## When to Use / When Not

- Use: SaaS landing, feature sections, pricing support, portfolios, changelogs-as-marketing, AI product pages.
- Don't: dashboards (use Swiss/Linear), long reading (use Editorial), dense admin tools.

## CSS Tokens

Reference: [references/tokens.css](references/tokens.css)

```css
@import 'references/tokens.css';

.bn-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 2fr 1fr 1fr;
  gap: 1rem;
}
.bn-cell {
  background: var(--bn-surface);
  border: var(--bn-border);
  border-radius: var(--bn-radius);
  padding: 1.75rem;
  overflow: hidden;
  position: relative;
}
```

## Component Examples

### Bento Grid

```css
.bn-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 2fr 1fr 1fr;
  grid-auto-rows: minmax(220px, auto);
  gap: 1rem;
  max-width: 1200px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 0 1.5rem;
}
.bn-cell {
  background: var(--bn-surface);
  border: var(--bn-border);
  border-radius: var(--bn-radius);
  padding: 1.75rem;
  overflow: hidden;
  position: relative;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  justify-content: flex-end;
}
.bn-cell-hero {
  grid-column: span 2;
  grid-row: span 2;
  min-height: 460px;
}
.bn-cell-tall {
  grid-row: span 2;
}
.bn-cell-wide {
  grid-column: span 2;
}
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .bn-grid {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
  .bn-cell-hero, .bn-cell-tall, .bn-cell-wide {
    grid-column: auto;
    grid-row: auto;
    min-height: 0;
  }
}
```

### Cell Variants (pick 2–3 per grid)

```css
/* Image cell */
.bn-cell-media {
  padding: 0;
}
.bn-cell-media img {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  object-fit: cover;
  display: block;
}

/* Gradient cell */
.bn-cell-gradient {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--bn-accent), var(--bn-accent-deep));
  color: #fff;
  border: none;
}

/* Code cell */
.bn-cell-code {
  background: var(--bn-ink);
  color: var(--bn-code-text);
  font-family: var(--bn-font-mono);
  font-size: 0.8125rem;
  justify-content: flex-start;
}
.bn-cell-code pre {
  margin: 0;
  overflow-x: auto;
}

/* Metric cell (real data only) */
.bn-cell-metric .bn-number {
  font-size: 2.5rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

/* CTA cell */
.bn-cell-cta {
  background: var(--bn-ink);
  color: var(--bn-paper);
  border: none;
}
```

### Bento Button

```css
.bn-btn {
  background: var(--bn-ink);
  color: var(--bn-paper);
  border-radius: var(--bn-radius-pill);
  padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  font-size: 0.9375rem;
  border: none;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: transform 0.2s var(--bn-ease), box-shadow 0.2s ease;
}
.bn-btn:hover {
  transform: translateY(-2px);
  box-shadow: var(--bn-shadow-lift);
}
.bn-btn:active {
  transform: translateY(0);
}
```

### Logo Wall (under hero, never inside)

```css
.bn-logos {
  display: flex;
  gap: 2.5rem;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  padding: 2rem 0;
  opacity: 0.7;
}
.bn-logos svg {
  height: 24px;
  width: auto;
}
/* Real SVG logos only (Simple Icons / devicon / generated marks). No plain-text wordmarks. */
```

## Hero Discipline

- Headline ≤ 2 lines, subtext ≤ 20 words AND ≤ 4 lines, CTA visible without scroll.
- Max 4 text elements in hero (brand strip OR eyebrow, headline, subtext, CTAs). No tagline below CTAs.
- Hero top padding max `pt-24` desktop; content never floats mid-viewport.
- No duplicate CTA intent on the page ("Get in touch" + "Let's talk" = fail).

## Typography

- Display sans, tight (`-0.03em`), cells use `1.25–1.5rem` headlines, hero `2.5–4rem`.
- Mono for code/metric cells only.

## Accessibility Notes

- Gradient/image cells: text contrast ≥ 4.5:1 — add scrim (`linear-gradient(transparent, rgba(0,0,0,0.6))`) behind bottom-anchored text.
- Grid reorders visually — keep DOM order logical for screen readers; don't use `order` to shuffle meaning.
- Motion: cell entrances stagger via `animation-delay` cascade, transform + opacity only, honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.

```css
.bn-cell-text-over-media::after {
  content: '';
  position: absolute;
  inset: auto 0 0 0;
  height: 60%;
  background: linear-gradient(transparent, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55));
  pointer-events: none;
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .bn-btn:hover {
    transform: none;
  }
}
```

---
name: claymorphism
description: Claymorphism design system skill. Use when building soft, puffy, clay-like UI components with large radii, dual inner shadows, and offset outer shadows.
license: MIT
user-invocable: false
disable-model-invocation: false
---

# Claymorphism Design Spec

## 3 Core Elements

1. **Large Radius** — Generous `border-radius` (20–50px) for a puffy, inflated look
2. **Dual Inner Shadows** — Light inset from top-left + dark inset from bottom-right to simulate 3D clay surface
3. **Offset Outer Shadow** — Directional `box-shadow` offset (not centered) to ground the element

## CSS Tokens

Reference: [references/tokens.css](references/tokens.css)

```css
@import 'references/tokens.css';

.clay-card {
  background: var(--clay-bg-card);
  border-radius: var(--clay-radius-lg);
  box-shadow: var(--clay-shadow);
  color: var(--clay-text);
}
```

## Component Examples

### Card
```css
.clay-card {
  background: var(--clay-bg-card);
  border-radius: var(--clay-radius-lg);
  box-shadow: var(--clay-shadow);
  padding: 1.5rem;
  color: var(--clay-text);
}
```

### Button
```css
.clay-btn {
  background: var(--clay-bg-button);
  border: none;
  border-radius: var(--clay-radius-pill);
  box-shadow: var(--clay-shadow);
  padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
  color: var(--clay-text);
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: box-shadow 0.2s;
}
.clay-btn:hover {
  box-shadow: var(--clay-shadow-elevated);
}
.clay-btn:active {
  box-shadow: var(--clay-shadow-pressed);
}
```

### Input
```css
.clay-input {
  background: var(--clay-bg);
  border: none;
  border-radius: var(--clay-radius);
  box-shadow: var(--clay-shadow-pressed);
  padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
  color: var(--clay-text);
}
.clay-input:focus {
  outline: 2px solid var(--clay-accent);
  outline-offset: 2px;
}
```

### Toggle
```css
.clay-toggle {
  width: 56px;
  height: 30px;
  background: var(--clay-bg-card);
  border-radius: var(--clay-radius-pill);
  box-shadow: var(--clay-shadow-pressed);
}
.clay-toggle-knob {
  width: 24px;
  height: 24px;
  background: var(--clay-bg);
  border-radius: 50%;
  box-shadow: var(--clay-shadow);
  transition: transform 0.2s;
}
```

## Dark Mode Notes

- Dark mode reduces inner highlight intensity (`rgba(255,255,255,0.05)` vs `0.6`) to avoid glowing artifacts
- Outer shadow opacity increases to maintain depth on dark backgrounds
- Background colors shift to warm dark tones — avoid pure black to preserve the clay feel
- All dark tokens are defined in `[data-theme="dark"]` in `tokens.css`

## Accessibility Notes

- Ensure **contrast ratio ≥ 4.5:1** for text — clay backgrounds are muted, verify against `--clay-text`
- Provide visible `:focus` outlines since clay shadows alone don't indicate focus
- Use `prefers-contrast: more` to flatten shadows and increase text contrast

```css
@media (prefers-contrast: more) {
  .clay-card {
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--clay-text);
  }
}
```

---
name: editorial
description: Editorial / magazine design system skill. Use when building reading-first UI with serif display type, drop caps, pull quotes, multi-column rhythm, and print-inspired hierarchy.
license: MIT
user-invocable: false
disable-model-invocation: false
---

# Editorial Design Spec

Magazine / journal / long-form reading. Type is the interface; whitespace is the interaction.

## Core Principles

1. **Serif Display + Sans Body** — Display serif (Newsreader, Source Serif, Fraunces, Playfair) for headlines; neutral sans for UI chrome and captions. Never reverse this.
2. **Measure & Rhythm** — Body measure `60–75ch`, line-height `1.7–1.8`, paragraph spacing ≥ `1.25em`. One idea per paragraph.
3. **Print Devices** — Drop caps on openers, pull quotes, kickers (ONE per article, not per section), folios (page footers), rules between features.
4. **Restrained Palette** — Paper white / ink black + one signature color. Photography carries the color, not chrome.
5. **Quiet Chrome** — Nav, buttons, and controls recede. No pill buttons shouting in an essay.

## When to Use / When Not

- Use: blogs, docs, newsletters, changelogs, portfolios, brand stories, help centers.
- Don't: dashboards, data tables, dense tools (use Swiss/Linear), playful apps (use Bento).

## CSS Tokens

Reference: [references/tokens.css](references/tokens.css)

```css
@import 'references/tokens.css';

.ed-article {
  max-width: var(--ed-measure);
  margin: 0 auto;
  font-family: var(--ed-serif);
}
```

## Component Examples

### Article Body

```css
.ed-article {
  max-width: var(--ed-measure);
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 0 1.5rem;
}
.ed-article p {
  font-family: var(--ed-serif);
  font-size: 1.125rem;
  line-height: 1.8;
  margin-bottom: 1.5em;
  color: var(--ed-ink);
}
.ed-article p:first-of-type::first-letter {
  font-size: 3.4em;
  float: left;
  line-height: 0.9;
  padding-right: 0.12em;
  font-weight: 600;
}
```

### Headline Stack

```css
.ed-kicker {
  font-family: var(--ed-sans);
  font-size: 0.75rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ed-accent);
}
.ed-headline {
  font-family: var(--ed-serif);
  font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 4vw + 1rem, 3.75rem);
  line-height: 1.08;
  letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  font-weight: 600;
  margin: 0.75rem 0 1rem;
}
.ed-dek {
  font-family: var(--ed-serif);
  font-size: 1.25rem;
  line-height: 1.55;
  color: var(--ed-muted);
  font-style: italic;
}
.ed-byline {
  font-family: var(--ed-sans);
  font-size: 0.8125rem;
  color: var(--ed-muted);
  border-top: var(--ed-rule);
  border-bottom: var(--ed-rule);
  padding: 0.75rem 0;
  margin: 1.5rem 0 2.5rem;
  display: flex;
  gap: 1rem;
}
```

### Pull Quote

```css
.ed-pullquote {
  font-family: var(--ed-serif);
  font-size: 1.625rem;
  line-height: 1.4;
  font-style: italic;
  border-left: 3px solid var(--ed-accent);
  padding-left: 1.5rem;
  margin: 2.5rem 0;
  color: var(--ed-ink);
}
```

### Quiet Button

```css
.ed-btn {
  background: transparent;
  color: var(--ed-ink);
  border: 1px solid var(--ed-ink);
  border-radius: var(--ed-radius);
  padding: 0.625rem 1.25rem;
  font-family: var(--ed-sans);
  font-size: 0.875rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: background 0.15s ease, color 0.15s ease;
}
.ed-btn:hover {
  background: var(--ed-ink);
  color: var(--ed-paper);
}
```

### Footnote / Caption

```css
.ed-caption {
  font-family: var(--ed-sans);
  font-size: 0.8125rem;
  line-height: 1.6;
  color: var(--ed-muted);
}
.ed-footnote {
  font-family: var(--ed-sans);
  font-size: 0.875rem;
  border-top: var(--ed-rule);
  padding-top: 1rem;
  margin-top: 3rem;
}
```

## Typography

- Display: serif, `600` weight, tight leading (`1.05–1.15`), slight negative tracking.
- Body: serif `400`, `1.125rem / 1.8`. UI chrome: sans `400–600`.
- Never set body in all-caps, never letterspace body copy.

## Accessibility Notes

- Serif body needs MORE line-height than sans (`1.7+`); don't go below `1.125rem` for article text.
- Italic dek + pull quotes: ensure contrast ≥ 4.5:1 (muted grays often fail — check).
- Drop caps must not break screen readers (use `::first-letter`, not extra markup).
- Long-form: honor `prefers-reduced-motion` for scroll-driven reveals; provide a `font-size` control or respect user scaling.

```css
@media (prefers-contrast: more) {
  .ed-dek, .ed-caption, .ed-byline {
    color: var(--ed-ink);
  }
}
```

---
name: glassmorphism
description: Glassmorphism design system skill. Use when building frosted-glass UI components with blur, transparency, and layered depth effects.
license: MIT
user-invocable: false
disable-model-invocation: false
---

# Glassmorphism Design Spec

## 4 Core Elements

1. **Transparency** — Semi-transparent backgrounds using `rgba()` or `hsla()` with alpha `0.05–0.4`
2. **Blur** — `backdrop-filter: blur()` ranging 8–40px for frosted-glass effect
3. **Border** — Subtle semi-transparent borders (`1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18)`) to define edges
4. **Shadow** — Soft layered `box-shadow` for depth separation from background

## CSS Tokens

Reference: [references/tokens.css](references/tokens.css)

Use CSS custom properties from `tokens.css` for consistent theming:

```css
@import 'references/tokens.css';

.glass-card {
  background: var(--glass-bg);
  backdrop-filter: var(--glass-blur);
  -webkit-backdrop-filter: var(--glass-blur);
  border: var(--glass-border);
  border-radius: var(--glass-radius);
  box-shadow: var(--glass-shadow);
}
```

## Component Examples

### Card
```css
.glass-card {
  background: var(--glass-bg);
  backdrop-filter: var(--glass-blur);
  -webkit-backdrop-filter: var(--glass-blur);
  border: var(--glass-border);
  border-radius: var(--glass-radius);
  box-shadow: var(--glass-shadow);
  padding: 1.5rem;
}
```

### Navbar
```css
.glass-nav {
  background: var(--glass-bg-heavy);
  backdrop-filter: var(--glass-blur-strong);
  -webkit-backdrop-filter: var(--glass-blur-strong);
  border-bottom: var(--glass-border);
  box-shadow: var(--glass-shadow);
  position: sticky;
  top: 0;
  z-index: 100;
}
```

### Modal Overlay
```css
.glass-modal-backdrop {
  background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
  backdrop-filter: blur(4px);
}
.glass-modal {
  background: var(--glass-bg-heavy);
  backdrop-filter: var(--glass-blur-strong);
  -webkit-backdrop-filter: var(--glass-blur-strong);
  border: var(--glass-border);
  border-radius: var(--glass-radius-lg);
  box-shadow: var(--glass-shadow-elevated);
}
```

### Button
```css
.glass-btn {
  background: var(--glass-bg-light);
  backdrop-filter: var(--glass-blur-light);
  -webkit-backdrop-filter: var(--glass-blur-light);
  border: var(--glass-border);
  border-radius: var(--glass-radius);
  transition: background 0.2s;
}
.glass-btn:hover {
  background: var(--glass-bg);
}
```

## Browser Compatibility

| Feature | Chrome | Firefox | Safari | Edge |
|---------|--------|---------|--------|------|
| `backdrop-filter` | 76+ | 103+ | 9+ (`-webkit-`) | 79+ |
| `rgba()` backgrounds | All | All | All | All |

- Always include `-webkit-backdrop-filter` for Safari support
- Firefox <103: use `@supports` fallback with solid semi-transparent bg
- Fallback pattern:

```css
.glass-card {
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85); /* fallback */
}
@supports (backdrop-filter: blur(1px)) {
  .glass-card {
    background: var(--glass-bg);
    backdrop-filter: var(--glass-blur);
  }
}
```

## Accessibility Notes

- Ensure **contrast ratio ≥ 4.5:1** for text over glass surfaces — test against all possible backgrounds
- Provide `prefers-reduced-transparency` media query to disable blur/transparency for users who need it
- Avoid placing critical text on highly transparent surfaces without a fallback
- Use `prefers-contrast: more` to increase border opacity and reduce transparency

```css
@media (prefers-reduced-transparency: reduce) {
  .glass-card {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92);
    backdrop-filter: none;
  }
}
@media (prefers-contrast: more) {
  .glass-card {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
    border: 1px solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
  }
}
```

---
name: linear-style
description: Linear/Vercel-style dark premium design system skill. Use when building developer tools, dashboards, and SaaS with dark-first surfaces, subtle borders, command-palette UX, and restrained glow.
license: MIT
user-invocable: false
disable-model-invocation: false
---

# Linear-Style Design Spec

Dark-premium developer aesthetic (Linear, Vercel, Raycast, Supabase): near-black surfaces, hairline borders, keyboard-first UX, motion that feels instant.

> Name note: directory is `linear-style` (not `linear`) to avoid confusion with CSS `linear-gradient`. Skill name: `linear-style`.

## Core Principles

1. **Dark First** — Design in dark, then backfill light. Surfaces: `#08090a` → `#0e0f11` → `#16181d`. Never pure `#000` + pure `#fff` text (use `#ededed`).
2. **Borders Over Shadows** — `1px rgba(255,255,255,0.08)` strokes define elevation. Shadows are near-invisible. No colored glow except ONE accent moment.
3. **Keyboard-First UX** — Command palette (`⌘K`), slash commands, visible shortcuts, focus that never gets lost. Every mouse flow has a keyboard path.
4. **Instant Motion** — `100–200ms`, `ease-out`, opacity + transform only. UI must feel faster than the user, never cinematic.
5. **Muted Everything, One Accent** — Grays do the work (`#8a8f98` secondary, `#62666d` tertiary). Accent (often `#5e6ad2` blurple or `#0070f3`) appears on active states and CTAs only.

## When to Use / When Not

- Use: dev tools, dashboards, SaaS, admin, CLI companions, AI products, settings, changelogs.
- Don't: marketing landing (use Bento/Editorial), playful consumer, luxury (use Editorial), print-like reading.

## CSS Tokens

Reference: [references/tokens.css](references/tokens.css)

```css
@import 'references/tokens.css';

.ln-card {
  background: var(--ln-raised);
  border: var(--ln-border);
  border-radius: var(--ln-radius);
}
```

## Component Examples

### Card / Panel

```css
.ln-card {
  background: var(--ln-raised);
  border: var(--ln-border);
  border-radius: var(--ln-radius);
  padding: 1.25rem;
}
.ln-card-hover:hover {
  background: var(--ln-overlay);
  border-color: var(--ln-border-strong);
}
```

### Button

```css
.ln-btn {
  background: var(--ln-accent);
  color: #fff;
  border: 1px solid transparent;
  border-radius: var(--ln-radius-sm);
  padding: 0.4375rem 0.875rem;
  font-family: var(--ln-font);
  font-size: 0.8125rem;
  font-weight: 500;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: background 0.12s ease, transform 0.12s ease;
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px rgba(255,255,255,0.08) inset;
}
.ln-btn:hover {
  background: var(--ln-accent-hover);
}
.ln-btn:active {
  transform: scale(0.98);
}
.ln-btn-ghost {
  background: transparent;
  color: var(--ln-text);
  border: var(--ln-border);
  box-shadow: none;
}
.ln-btn-ghost:hover {
  background: var(--ln-overlay);
}
```

### Command Palette

```css
.ln-palette-backdrop {
  background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);
  backdrop-filter: blur(2px);
}
.ln-palette {
  background: var(--ln-raised);
  border: var(--ln-border-strong);
  border-radius: var(--ln-radius-lg);
  box-shadow: 0 24px 64px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
  max-width: 640px;
  overflow: hidden;
}
.ln-palette-input {
  background: transparent;
  border: none;
  border-bottom: var(--ln-border);
  padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
  font-size: 0.9375rem;
  color: var(--ln-text);
  width: 100%;
}
.ln-palette-item {
  padding: 0.625rem 1.25rem;
  display: flex;
  gap: 0.75rem;
  align-items: center;
  font-size: 0.875rem;
}
.ln-palette-item[aria-selected="true"] {
  background: var(--ln-overlay);
}
.ln-kbd {
  font-family: var(--ln-font-mono);
  font-size: 0.75rem;
  background: var(--ln-overlay);
  border: var(--ln-border);
  border-radius: 4px;
  padding: 0.125rem 0.375rem;
  color: var(--ln-muted);
}
```

### Sidebar Nav

```css
.ln-sidebar {
  background: var(--ln-base);
  border-right: var(--ln-border);
  width: 240px;
  padding: 0.75rem;
}
.ln-sidebar-item {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.625rem;
  padding: 0.4375rem 0.625rem;
  border-radius: var(--ln-radius-sm);
  font-size: 0.8125rem;
  color: var(--ln-muted);
}
.ln-sidebar-item:hover {
  background: var(--ln-overlay);
  color: var(--ln-text);
}
.ln-sidebar-item[aria-current="page"] {
  background: var(--ln-overlay);
  color: var(--ln-text);
}
```

### Status / Dot

```css
/* Semantic dots allowed here (unlike marketing) — small, real state only */
.ln-dot {
  width: 8px;
  height: 8px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: var(--ln-success);
}
.ln-dot-pulse {
  animation: ln-pulse 2s ease-in-out infinite;
}
@keyframes ln-pulse {
  50% { opacity: 0.4; }
}
```

### Input

```css
.ln-input {
  background: var(--ln-base);
  border: var(--ln-border);
  border-radius: var(--ln-radius-sm);
  padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
  font-size: 0.8125rem;
  color: var(--ln-text);
}
.ln-input:focus {
  outline: none;
  border-color: var(--ln-accent);
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px var(--ln-accent-soft);
}
.ln-input::placeholder {
  color: var(--ln-faint);
}
```

## Typography

- Sans only (Inter / Geist), `13–14px` UI text, tight headings.
- Mono for IDs, shortcuts, numbers, code.
- Never serif here.

## Motion

```css
:root {
  --ln-ease: cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
}
.ln-fade-in {
  animation: ln-in 0.15s var(--ln-ease) both;
}
@keyframes ln-in {
  from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(4px) scale(0.98); }
  to { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
}
```

## Accessibility Notes

- Dark grays fail fast: secondary text must be ≥ `#9ca3af`-equivalent on dark; check 4.5:1 for body, 3:1 for large/secondary.
- Focus-visible ring in accent on EVERY interactive element; command palette traps + returns focus.
- `prefers-reduced-motion`: kill pulse/fade, keep instant state changes.
- Dual-mode is mandatory: every token has a light twin in `tokens.css`; test both before ship.

```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .ln-dot-pulse, .ln-fade-in {
    animation: none;
  }
}
```

