# Swiss Design Spec

International Typographic Style: grid-first, type-led, ultra-restrained. The most reliable "premium default" for fintech, enterprise, SaaS, docs.

## Core Principles

1. **Grid First** — 12-column grid, mathematical spacing, everything aligns to the grid. No floating elements.
2. **Typography Is the Design** — One grotesque family (Inter, Helvetica Now, Neue Haas, Geist, IBM Plex Sans). Size + weight + tracking create hierarchy, not color or decoration.
3. **Asymmetric Balance** — Left-aligned headlines, generous whitespace, content offset from center. Massive empty zones are intentional.
4. **Restrained Color** — Black/white/gray + ONE accent (often blue, red, or electric). No gradients, no shadows-as-decoration.
5. **Flat & Precise** — Hairline dividers (`1px`), sharp or tiny radius (`0–6px`), no blur, no glass.

## When to Use / When Not

- Use: fintech, enterprise SaaS, dashboards, docs, admin, data-dense tools, B2B landing.
- Don't: playful consumer, gaming, kids, luxury editorial (use Editorial instead), expressive marketing (use Bento instead).

## CSS Tokens

Reference: [references/tokens.css](references/tokens.css)

```css
@import 'references/tokens.css';

.sw-card {
  background: var(--sw-surface);
  border: var(--sw-border);
  border-radius: var(--sw-radius);
  padding: 1.5rem;
}
```

## Component Examples

### Card

```css
.sw-card {
  background: var(--sw-surface);
  border: var(--sw-border);
  border-radius: var(--sw-radius);
  padding: 1.5rem;
}
.sw-card + .sw-card {
  margin-top: 1px; /* hairline stacking, not shadows */
}
```

### Button

```css
.sw-btn {
  background: var(--sw-ink);
  color: var(--sw-paper);
  border: 1px solid var(--sw-ink);
  border-radius: var(--sw-radius);
  padding: 0.625rem 1.25rem;
  font-family: var(--sw-font);
  font-weight: 600;
  font-size: 0.875rem;
  letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: background 0.15s ease, color 0.15s ease;
}
.sw-btn:hover {
  background: var(--sw-accent);
  border-color: var(--sw-accent);
}
.sw-btn:active {
  transform: translateY(1px);
}
.sw-btn-secondary {
  background: transparent;
  color: var(--sw-ink);
}
.sw-btn:focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid var(--sw-accent);
  outline-offset: 2px;
}
```

### Navbar

```css
.sw-nav {
  background: var(--sw-paper);
  border-bottom: var(--sw-border);
  padding: 0 2rem;
  height: 60px;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 2rem;
  position: sticky;
  top: 0;
  z-index: 100;
}
```

### Data Table

```css
.sw-table {
  width: 100%;
  border-collapse: collapse;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}
.sw-table th {
  font-size: 0.75rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  color: var(--sw-muted);
  text-align: left;
  padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
  border-bottom: var(--sw-border-strong);
}
.sw-table td {
  padding: 0.875rem 1rem;
  border-bottom: var(--sw-border);
  font-size: 0.875rem;
}
.sw-table tr:hover td {
  background: var(--sw-wash);
}
.sw-table td.num {
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  text-align: right;
}
```

### Input

```css
.sw-input {
  background: var(--sw-paper);
  border: var(--sw-border);
  border-radius: var(--sw-radius);
  padding: 0.625rem 0.875rem;
  font-family: var(--sw-font);
  font-size: 0.875rem;
}
.sw-input:focus {
  outline: none;
  border-color: var(--sw-accent);
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px var(--sw-accent-soft);
}
```

## Typography

- One family only. Headings tight tracking (`-0.03em` display, `-0.02em` h2), body neutral.
- Display numbers: `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`, tight leading.
- Uppercase micro-labels: sparing — max one per view, never on every section (see `design-taste/reference/anti-slop.md`).

```css
h1, h2, h3 {
  font-family: var(--sw-font);
  letter-spacing: var(--sw-tracking-tight);
  font-weight: 700;
}
body {
  font-family: var(--sw-font);
  font-size: 0.9375rem;
  line-height: 1.6;
  color: var(--sw-ink);
  background: var(--sw-paper);
}
```

## Layout

```css
.sw-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(12, 1fr);
  gap: 1.5rem;
  max-width: 1200px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 0 2rem;
}
.sw-hero {
  text-align: left; /* never center long-form */
  padding: 6rem 0 4rem;
  max-width: 44rem;
}
```

## Accessibility Notes

- Hairlines (`#e5e5e5` on white) fail as sole separators for low-vision — pair with spacing + type contrast.
- Accent-on-white must hit 4.5:1 for body text; use darker accent ramp for text.
- Focus rings always visible (`:focus-visible` 2px accent).
- Numbers in tables: `tabular-nums` + right-align to avoid jitter.

```css
@media (prefers-contrast: more) {
  .sw-card {
    border-width: 2px;
  }
}
```

